    "fullDesc": "Understand how AI agents can interpret tasks, access approved tools, retrieve relevant information and perform controlled multi-step workflows.\n\nThis practical AI Agents Fundamentals course introduces agentic AI concepts, single-agent architecture, context management, structured outputs, function calling, API integrations and safe execution boundaries.\n\nLearn how tool-using agents differ from ordinary chatbots and rule-based automation systems, and identify when agent-based solutions are appropriate for business tasks.\n\nGain supervised experience using OpenAI's supported agent tooling or an equivalent visual agent builder, alongside introductory n8n AI Agent tools.\n\nExplore approved information retrieval, task routing, tool selection, input validation, human approvals and basic error handling.\n\nDevelop foundational skills in prompt-injection awareness, permissions, output verification, execution tracing and agent evaluation using realistic test scenarios.\n\nComplete two supervised agent prototypes: a business information assistant that produces traceable answers and a task-routing agent that chooses among allowed actions while requiring approval for sensitive operations.\n\nBuild a 15-case evaluation dataset to test correct behavior, tool selection, access restrictions, prompt-injection resistance and recovery.\n\nThe programme focuses on safe, understandable and testable agent prototypes rather than enterprise autonomous systems, complex multi-agent orchestration or production infrastructure engineering.",
