    "shortDesc": "Learn AI-assisted market, business and academic research using modern research platforms. Master source discovery, evidence verification, document comparison, citation tracing and professional research reporting.",
    "fullDesc": "Learn how to conduct more structured, efficient and trustworthy research using AI-assisted discovery tools, academic search platforms and source-grounded document analysis.\n\nThis practical AI Research & Evidence Verification course teaches research question design, search strategies, market and competitor intelligence, academic literature discovery, source credibility assessment and evidence-based reporting.\n\nDevelop hands-on experience with Perplexity, Gemini Notebook, Google Scholar and either Consensus or Elicit as the cohort's principal academic AI research platform.\n\nExplore ChatGPT or Gemini Deep Research, Semantic Scholar, Google Sheets and citation management tools as relevant supporting resources.\n\nLearn how to distinguish original evidence from secondary reporting, assess research methodology, check factual claims, trace citations, identify conflicting findings and record uncertainty.\n\nWork with PDFs and multiple sources to extract information, compare documents and develop transparent evidence matrices.\n\nBuild two professional research reports: a market and competitive intelligence report with actionable business recommendations, and an academic or industry literature review demonstrating study comparison, source-quality assessment and properly traceable references.\n\nThe programme focuses on responsible research discovery, evaluation, synthesis and professional communication—not advanced statistics, formal systematic-review certification or replacing qualified researchers.",
