    "shortDesc": "Learn professional user interface design in Figma. Build responsive website and mobile app screens using Auto Layout, reusable components, design tokens, clickable prototypes and developer-ready handoff practices.",
    "fullDesc": "Learn how to design professional, responsive and interactive digital interfaces using Figma. This practical Figma UI Design & Responsive Prototyping course develops hands-on skills in interface layout, visual hierarchy, spacing systems, typography, wireframes, responsive design, component libraries and interactive prototypes. Master Figma's Auto Layout capabilities, including horizontal, vertical and grid layouts; Hug Contents, Fill Container, Fixed sizing, min/max dimensions, wrapping and nested component behavior. Learn to create adaptable website structures, responsive product cards, desktop and mobile navigation patterns, reusable UI components, variants, design styles and design tokens. Develop foundational knowledge of accessibility, contrast, target sizing, readable typography and consistent interaction states. Build practical skills in designing multi-screen e-commerce interfaces, mobile app flows, navigation interactions, overlays, interactive components and realistic prototype demonstrations. Explore Figma variables, reusable design libraries, light/dark modes and documented UI systems that support consistent design across multiple screens. Learn how to prepare organized design files, reusable assets, component specifications, responsive behavior notes and developer-ready handoff documentation. Complete a professional portfolio containing a responsive e-commerce website, a mobile app flow with at least five meaningful screens, a reusable component library, a clickable prototype and a documented developer handoff. The programme emphasizes genuine responsive behavior, professional interface craftsmanship, systematic component reuse and practical UI delivery. It is a focused UI production specialization, not a replacement for a longer programme covering comprehensive UX research, usability testing and product strategy.",
