    "learningOutcomes": [
      "Design clean, structurally disciplined user interfaces in Figma applying optical alignment, visual hierarchy, 8pt spacing grids, and typography systems.",
      "Translate business briefs and user goals into low-fidelity wireframes, screen architectures, and state flows (empty, loading, error, success) in FigJam.",
      "Master Auto Layout mechanics—Hug Contents, Fill Container, Fixed sizing, min/max dimensions, and auto-spacing—to build layouts that genuinely adapt to viewport changes.",
      "Construct responsive components including adaptive headers, multi-column product grids, and self-adjusting cards that pass rigorous manual width stress tests (1440px to 320px).",
      "Build a production-grade Reusable UI Component Library with variants, boolean properties, instance swaps, and primitive vs semantic design tokens.",
      "Implement multi-theme UI systems using Figma variables and modes, supporting seamless toggling between Light and Dark interface themes.",
      "Create realistic interactive prototypes featuring multi-screen user flows, modal overlays, mobile navigation drawers, and polished micro-interactions.",
      "Conduct UI accessibility audits verifying WCAG color contrast ratios, minimum 44×44px interactive touch targets, and accessible form labels.",
      "Deliver developer-ready handoff packages complete with standardized frame naming, spacing/typography specs, exportable SVG assets, and responsive behavior notes."
    ],
