    "title": "Logo Design & Vector Identity Marks",
    "shortTitle": "Logo Design & Vector Identity Marks",
    "shortDesc": "Learn professional logo design from client discovery and concept sketches to vector construction, typography, optical refinement and client-ready delivery. Create versatile marks for brands, products and digital applications.",
    "fullDesc": "Learn how to develop original, professional and versatile logo designs using Adobe Illustrator. This practical Logo Design & Vector Identity Marks course teaches the process of creating a logo, from understanding a client brief and exploring visual ideas to building precise vector artwork and preparing professional final files. Develop research-informed skills in identifying brand characteristics, evaluating competitor logos, exploring symbolism, generating original concepts and selecting visual directions. Learn creative techniques including mind mapping, thumbnail sketching, negative space, letterform exploration and geometric thinking. Master the Adobe Illustrator tools used in professional logo production, including the Pen Tool, Bézier curves, Shape Builder, Pathfinder, compound paths, typographic refinement and optical correction. Create symbol marks, wordmarks, lettermarks and combination marks with strong proportions, clean geometry and considered visual balance. Learn to refine logos through black-and-white testing, small-size legibility, favicon applications, light and dark backgrounds and practical usage contexts. Explore how primary, secondary and compact logo versions support flexible applications without expanding into a complete brand identity system. Build a professional portfolio containing three original logo concepts supported by research and sketches, two fully refined logo solutions, appropriate size and color variations, and a client-ready file delivery package. Learn introductory trademark similarity awareness and understand why professional legal clearance remains a separate process. The programme focuses on original concept development, vector precision, visual problem-solving and professional client delivery—not merely recreating existing logos or generating marks using templates.",
    "positioning": "Learn how to develop original, professional and versatile logo designs using Adobe Illustrator. This practical Logo Design & Vector Identity Marks course teaches the process of creating a logo, from understanding a client brief and exploring visual ideas to building precise vector artwork and preparing professional final files. Develop research-informed skills in identifying brand characteristics, evaluating competitor logos, exploring symbolism, generating original concepts and selecting visual directions. Learn creative techniques including mind mapping, thumbnail sketching, negative space, letterform exploration and geometric thinking. Master the Adobe Illustrator tools used in professional logo production, including the Pen Tool, Bézier curves, Shape Builder, Pathfinder, compound paths, typographic refinement and optical correction. Create symbol marks, wordmarks, lettermarks and combination marks with strong proportions, clean geometry and considered visual balance. Learn to refine logos through black-and-white testing, small-size legibility, favicon applications, light and dark backgrounds and practical usage contexts. Explore how primary, secondary and compact logo versions support flexible applications without expanding into a complete brand identity system. Build a professional portfolio containing three original logo concepts supported by research and sketches, two fully refined logo solutions, appropriate size and color variations, and a client-ready file delivery package. Learn introductory trademark similarity awareness and understand why professional legal clearance remains a separate process. The programme focuses on original concept development, vector precision, visual problem-solving and professional client delivery—not merely recreating existing logos or generating marks using templates.",
