    "fullDesc": "Learn how to build professional, responsive websites from scratch using HTML and CSS—without requiring previous coding experience.\n\nThis practical HTML, CSS & Responsive Web Design course starts with web fundamentals, semantic HTML, page structure, accessible content, links, images, tables and forms.\n\nDevelop professional CSS skills in selectors, the cascade, specificity, typography, spacing, colors, the box model, reusable styles and custom properties.\n\nMaster modern layout techniques using Flexbox, CSS Grid, relative units, responsive images, mobile-first design, media queries and container queries.\n\nLearn to build common website elements such as responsive navigation, hero sections, cards, galleries, buttons, contact forms and footers using clean HTML and CSS.\n\nExplore CSS transitions, carefully controlled animations, keyboard focus indicators and reduced-motion support.\n\nDevelop foundational knowledge of web accessibility, technical SEO, image optimization, Core Web Vitals and page testing.\n\nLearn to translate simple Figma layouts into HTML/CSS, debug websites using Chrome DevTools, organize source files and publish static sites with GitHub Pages.\n\nUse AI tools responsibly to explain code, identify possible CSS issues and review accessibility or responsiveness—while independently testing every suggested change.\n\nBuild two assessed portfolio projects: a responsive business landing page and a multi-page personal or professional portfolio website.\n\nBoth projects must demonstrate responsive layouts, essential keyboard accessibility, organized source code, clear documentation and deployment readiness.\n\nThe programme focuses on real HTML/CSS website development, not JavaScript application logic, React, authentication or backend programming.",
