    "fullDesc": "Learn to build practical backend systems using Node.js, Express and PostgreSQL. This hands-on Node.js Backend Development with Express course teaches server-side JavaScript, REST API development, relational database integration, authentication, authorization, testing and backend deployment. Start by understanding how Node.js operates outside the browser, how asynchronous I/O works, and how to use modules, npm, environment variables, filesystem operations and debugging tools. Develop HTTP APIs using Express. Learn routing, middleware, controllers, request and response handling, validation and structured error responses. Connect applications to PostgreSQL using a maintained Node.js database client. Build CRUD operations with parameterized SQL, database constraints, schema migrations, transactions and reliable connection management. Implement user authentication and practical backend security controls, including secure password hashing, session or token concepts, role checks, resource ownership verification, input validation and rate limiting. Develop an understanding of object-level authorization so authenticated users can access only records they are permitted to read or modify. Learn backend reliability through automated unit and integration tests, error handling, structured logging, environment separation, API documentation and debugging workflows. Complete a portfolio-ready business operations REST API featuring a PostgreSQL database, authenticated users, protected CRUD operations, authorization tests and a deployable demonstration. This programme emphasizes maintainable code, correct API behavior, database reliability, security fundamentals and working technical evidence.",
