    "learningOutcomes": [
      "Understand relational database architecture, tables, schemas, and select appropriate PostgreSQL data types for business entities.",
      "Write accurate SQL queries to retrieve, filter, sort, and project structured data using SELECT, WHERE, ORDER BY, LIMIT, and DISTINCT.",
      "Handle NULL values correctly using IS NULL, IS NOT NULL, and COALESCE functions within three-valued logic rules.",
      "Model entities and combine datasets across multiple tables using Primary Keys, Foreign Keys, INNER JOIN, and LEFT JOIN without row duplication.",
      "Aggregate and analyze business records using COUNT, SUM, AVG, MIN, MAX, GROUP BY, and HAVING to produce summary reports.",
      "Implement conditional business logic with CASE expressions and construct readable multi-step queries using subqueries and CTEs (WITH).",
      "Apply introductory window functions (ROW_NUMBER, RANK, running totals) to rank business records while preserving row detail.",
      "Create and modify relational schemas using CREATE/ALTER TABLE with constraints, perform safe data modifications, and execute ACID transactions."
    ],
