    "learningOutcomes": [
      "Explain the foundational accounting equation (Assets = Liabilities + Equity) and its operational significance in business bookkeeping.",
      "Apply universal double-entry rules of debit and credit across real-world commercial transactions.",
      "Construct accurate journal entries with complete debits, credits, proper accounts, and descriptive narrations.",
      "Post journal entries to general and subsidiary ledgers and compute ongoing debit or credit balances.",
      "Prepare and interpret a trial balance to verify the mathematical agreement of debits and credits.",
      "Understand basic accrual accounting principles, revenue recognition timing, and expense matching concepts.",
      "Identify and inspect primary business source documents including tax invoices, purchase bills, payment receipts, vouchers, and bank statements.",
      "Navigate the TallyPrime interface proficiently using the Gateway of Tally, top menus, and standard keyboard shortcuts.",
      "Create a fictional registered business company profile in TallyPrime with appropriate state jurisdiction, currency, and books-beginning dates.",
      "Configure multi-year financial accounting periods, reporting dates, and transactional period locks in TallyPrime.",
      "Create and organize ledger groups into primary groups and sub-groups adhering to standard Indian accounting standards.",
      "Build a comprehensive, logical chart of accounts tailored to a commercial trading entity.",
      "Create accounting ledger masters for capital, bank, cash, suppliers, customers, sales, purchases, and operating expenses.",
      "Record customer receipts, advances, and other business inflows accurately using Receipt Vouchers.",
      "Record supplier disbursements, operational expenses, and statutory fees accurately using Payment Vouchers.",
      "Record internal cash-to-bank deposits, bank-to-cash withdrawals, and inter-bank transfers using Contra Vouchers.",
      "Record non-cash adjustments, depreciation entries, period-end accruals, and rectifications using Journal Vouchers.",
      "Record credit and cash inventory purchases against supplier invoices using Purchase Vouchers in item invoice mode.",
      "Record credit and cash customer sales with automated tax calculation using Sales Vouchers in item invoice mode.",
      "Create and record Debit Notes for purchase returns, supplier rate differences, and credit adjustments.",
      "Create and record Credit Notes for sales returns, post-sale volume discounts, and customer billing corrections.",
      "Configure stock groups and sub-groups to categorize trading merchandise effectively.",
      "Create stock item masters with descriptive codes, applicable tax classifications, standard costing, and reorder levels.",
      "Configure standard units of measure (UoM) including simple and compound units (e.g. Nos, Pcs, Kgs, Boxes).",
      "Set up multiple warehouses, stock godowns, and branch locations to manage storage and inventory movement.",
      "Record inter-godown inventory transfers, inward stock receipt notes, and outward delivery notes.",
      "Understand inventory valuation methods (FIFO, Weighted Average) and their direct impact on closing stock value and net profit.",
      "Execute complete procurement and sales order cycles connecting purchase orders, receipt notes, delivery notes, and final billing.",
      "Perform manual and automated bank reconciliation statements (BRS) to reconcile book balances with simulated bank statements.",
      "Configure and allocate operational expenses across functional Cost Centres and Cost Categories for internal management reporting.",
      "Read and interpret outstanding receivables ageing reports to monitor customer credit and collection cycles.",
      "Generate and interpret the Profit & Loss Account to evaluate trading gross margins and net operating profitability.",
      "Generate and interpret the Balance Sheet to evaluate business financial position, asset liquidity, and capital solvency.",
      "Systematically investigate, detect, and correct accounting errors, reversed entries, duplicate vouchers, and ledger misclassifications.",
      "Explain Indian GST registration concepts, GSTIN structure, threshold limits, and composition versus regular taxpayer schemes.",
      "Differentiate the statutory roles and calculation rules of Central GST (CGST), State GST (SGST), and Integrated GST (IGST).",
      "Determine the correct legal place of supply for goods and services to identify intrastate versus interstate tax applicability.",
      "Identify and assign appropriate Harmonized System of Nomenclature (HSN) and Service Accounting Code (SAC) classifications.",
      "Understand current official GST tax slabs (0%, 5%, 12%, 18%, 28%) and statutory exemption lists.",
      "Explain Reverse Charge Mechanism (RCM) awareness, recipient tax payment liabilities, and self-invoicing requirements.",
      "Prepare compliant GST tax invoices containing mandatory fields, tax breakdowns, HSN summaries, and dispatch details.",
      "Review credit and debit notes for GST reporting implications, original invoice linkage, and tax liability adjustments.",
      "Interpret and prepare GSTR-1 return reports covering B2B invoices, B2C sales, credit/debit notes, and HSN outward summaries.",
      "Prepare GSTR-3B monthly tax summary returns calculating net output tax liability, eligible input tax credit, and tax payment totals.",
      "Reconcile monthly purchase registers against auto-drafted GSTR-2B statements to identify ITC timing differences and mismatches.",
      "Perform systematic Input Tax Credit (ITC) matching and determine eligible versus ineligible credit under GST statutory rules.",
      "Explain Invoice Management System (IMS) functions: supplier invoice actions (Accept, Reject, Pending) and their effect on GSTR-2B.",
      "Explain electronic invoicing (e-Invoicing) eligibility criteria, statutory turnover thresholds, and exempted taxpayer categories.",
      "Understand Invoice Reference Number (IRN) generation workflows via authorized Invoice Registration Portals (IRP) and signed QR codes.",
      "Explain electronic way bill (e-Way Bill) applicability, mandatory movement thresholds, Part-A/Part-B data, and validity periods.",
      "Understand statutory audit-trail mandates, accounting edit logs, and the operational differences between TallyPrime and TallyPrime Edit Log.",
      "Execute secure company data backups, offsite archive procedures, and verified data restore drills.",
      "Review GST Annual Computation reports in TallyPrime Release 7.2 and export HSN summaries and return tables.",
      "Distinguish local GSTR-9 annual return data preparation and export from the separate statutory portal filing process.",
      "Process a comprehensive practical accounting simulation featuring at least 100 representative transactions across multiple periods.",
      "Reconcile trading accounts, physical inventory, bank statements, and GST returns across consecutive monthly reporting periods.",
      "Assemble, format, and present a professional Complete Simulated Trading-Business Accounting & GST Reconciliation Package.",
      "Articulate accounting discrepancies, document corrective adjustments, and operate within the legal boundaries of non-certified personnel."
    ],
